  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_10116c5bfe2946509c842014e8e6f27c",
      "statement": "filesScopeRestricted confines read-scope only for a logically remote caller (Tailscale serve, a trusted_networks peer, a phone); a direct-loopback caller's Files API reads are not confined to cwd/git root, because a direct-loopback connection is treated as equivalent to the OS user themself, who can already read any file via Explorer or through the wrapped AI CLI's own OS-level permissions, and POST /api/spawn already accepts provider=\"shell\" with only drive-root/home-directory rejected, so confining only Hub reads would not be a real boundary for that caller.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/hub/files_scope.go#L1-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4c5ad023a6424f34c384896cc8958d5630019d9194d984f324c0add44573ac8d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c24c6b9deeef47119f6f036fa54617c9",
      "statement": "Write operations (files-save/files-create/mkdir/move/rename/delete) never use filesScopeRestricted and stay confined to cwd/git-root regardless of connection kind, because the risk there is accidental corruption outside the user's own repository rather than a confidentiality boundary; secretReadDeniedExtensions (.pem, .key) and secretReadDeniedBasenames are blocked outright even within the allowed-roots read path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/hub/files_scope.go#L26-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5f49bbdf609f73977d6f571d3e923bd94f8f66c670bb64018ec3e044f657c3a3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_df79383371494edba1daabea7f4f76d6",
      "statement": "/api/files-content enforces a fixed allowlist of previewable text extensions and a 1 MiB size cap (filesContentMaxSize), and its response's ReadOnly flag distinguishes a normal in-scope read from one permitted only because the path was mentioned in chat and fell back to read-only access outside the allowed roots.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/hub/files_content.go#L16-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ea7c0f2370cef4ef10daf92b15a6d808c90d1f89559d62dbe363449a08af57e9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ada10dbd43644c6b85a463fa9071a648",
      "statement": "POST /api/files-save validates in order: token+method, absolute-path plus allowed-root scope, extension allowlist, a 1 MiB content size cap, that the target file exists and is not a directory (the endpoint never creates a new file), and finally, only if an optional baseMtime was supplied, compares it against the file's current on-disk mtime and returns 409 Conflict on a mismatch; the request body itself is separately capped at 2 MiB (filesSaveBodyMaxBytes) ahead of the narrower content check.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/hub/files_save.go#L12-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:49933101534b4c9f7a46078d3908969194120285ecc12355de11225a8ef95e5c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/hub/files_save.go#L36-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7ddf0ea57e2a6fffd6dae9a940ad083d46a6b69ab9d65c25618caa25931c0acf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fcc62ef085714636aa1daccac910a2dd",
      "statement": "atomicRenameNoReplace exists to fix a tracked defect (HUB-5) where a plain os.Rename succeeds even when the destination already exists, meaning files_move.go/files_rename.go's separate existence check before renaming left a TOCTOU gap that a concurrent writer could race, silently overwriting a destination created in between; the fix uses OS-specific fail-if-exists rename primitives so the check and rename become one atomic operation, and isRenameTargetExistsErr lets a caller map that specific failure to HTTP 409 Conflict.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/hub/atomic_rename.go#L1-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:852e68657a3a69b55f7ab31058cf01abfbe67823a0b0ca8612672b2510cf5032:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1a6e411fe2f94b1fa96418c547dcfc22",
      "statement": "The git-commit-all flow enforces bounded inputs: a commit subject capped at 200 characters (gitCommitSubjectMaxLen), a body capped at 8192 characters (gitCommitBodyMaxLen), and the diff shown for review truncated at 48 KiB (gitCommitDiffMaxBytes) when it exceeds that size.",
